INT. MOREAU CONSERVATORY OF GLASS - OBSERVATION GALLERY - NIGHT

A great glass dome shelters a jungle of tropical plants. Above, rain on the panes. Below, a long dining table laid with candles, crystal, and silver, at which six guests have gathered for a gala dinner.

CALISTA MOREAU, 50s, the hostess, in a ruby gown, presides at the head. BARTHOLOMEW "BART" QUINCE, 60s, the collector, red-faced and jovial, sits at her right. NAVEEN RAO, 40s, the insurance assessor, taps a pen against his wine glass. LUDMILA, 30s, a violinist, waits in her chair with the instrument in her lap. FERRIS, 40s, the butler, stands behind with a silver tray. ZHOU MEI, 30s, a restorer, studies the centerpiece, a small bronze sculpture on a pedestal of black marble.

CALISTA
Ladies and gentlemen. Dinner.

BART
At last.

NAVEEN
Before we eat, Mrs. Moreau, I'd like to confirm the sculpture's appraisal.

CALISTA
Four million.

NAVEEN
Four and a half, I believe, by the last estimate.

CALISTA
You are very precise.

NAVEEN
It is my profession.

ZHOU MEI
It's very beautiful.

BART
It is a fraud.

LUDMILA
Excuse me?

BART
The original is in a private vault in Zurich. I bought it myself. This is the copy.

CALISTA
You are wrong, Bartholomew.

BART
I am never wrong about bronzes.

FERRIS
Shall I pour, madam?

CALISTA
Please.

FERRIS
Very good.

NAVEEN
If it is a copy, the insurance is void.

ZHOU MEI
It is not a copy.

NAVEEN
How would you know?

ZHOU MEI
I restored it. I know every scratch.

BART
Then you are in on it.

ZHOU MEI
I am not in on anything.

LUDMILA
Someone play me a waltz. This is unbearable.

CALISTA
Ludmila, hush. Zhou Mei, if you restored it, what did you find on the base?

ZHOU MEI
A maker's mark. Three letters.

CALISTA
And what were they?

ZHOU MEI
C. M. R.

CALISTA
Calista Moreau, Restorer. My own mark.

BART
(slowly)
You made it. Yourself.

CALISTA
Thirty years ago. In this conservatory.

NAVEEN
Mrs. Moreau, do you understand what you're saying?

CALISTA
Perfectly. The Zurich bronze is the forgery, Bartholomew.

Bart stands. His chair crashes behind him.

BART
You sold me a fake.

CALISTA
Forty years ago. For a very good price.

FERRIS
Shall I call the police, madam?

CALISTA
Not yet, Ferris. Pour the wine.
